    "created_at": "2016-06-21T15:53:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-21T15:53:31Z",
    "body": "Why does the Firefox way (that is, treating it as a network error) require knowing supported protocols in advance?  I don't think it does.  Note that Firefox does NOT show a network error if we find an external application to handle the protocol, and I'm 99% sure we do that async.  Certainly nothing prevents it being done async in theory.\n\nThe Chrome way has the drawback that given `<a href=\"foopy:stuff\">click me</a>` the user clicks the link ... and nothing happens.  And there's no feedback as to _why_ nothing happened.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
