    "created_at": "2016-06-24T15:18:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-24T15:18:28Z",
    "body": "Hmm.  So Chrome stops the load on that testcase.  Firefox does not, looks like.\n\nFrom a user experience perspective not stopping is vastly better, of course...  on the other hand your example of protocol handlers implemented via navigating away entirely means the user experience is kinda sucky in somewhat unpredictable ways already.\n",
